      "writtenOn": "2024-07-01T20:26:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Also - note http://go/apis-native-and-idl and policy against using binder in API surfaces. It doesn\u0027t technically apply here as this is a platform API, but it will apply when AVF becomes updatable (and this will need to be systemapi), which we want to enable for the official servicemanagement APIs.\n\nThat\u0027s a good point... That prevents a callback like this from returning any binder at all? Even if we don\u0027t make any assumptions about the type in libbinder? The client is going to try and cast it to a type it expects, even if libbinder doesn\u0027t.\n\nJust noting my reasoning here for now, but I think the point above seems more important:\n\nI want to be able to reuse the code in libbinder that gets an accessor, retrieves the FD, and sets up the RPC binder connection underneath the libbinder service manager APIs.\n\nIn order to do that, I need to return an accessor to the code in libbinder. `android::os::Service` is what I\u0027d really like to return, but that can\u0027t work.\n\nIf we returned the service\u0027s binder instead, this callback code would need to repeat everything in libbinder for setting up the connection which I want to avoid.",
      "parentUuid": "8b4a9bcb_64a0c8c2",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 77,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 77,
        "endChar": 16
      },
      "revId": "5753132477c8ff12e0b092c670e9e719109d86c0",
